All 1,167 unresolved rows in the two one-edit families now have opposing
worlds. The remaining **279 bound gaps** belong to the partial timing
contracts, whose optional-object search is outside this follow-up. Their
universal intervals still straddle the decision, but a bound alone is not
proof of both attainable decisions. The 2,199 blocked rows remain blocked.
These rows overlap in images, cases, thresholds and families; they are not
independent evaluations or customer decisions.

An 8,404-binding freeze precedes the new searches. Eight controls include
56 synthetic case compositions and reject edited-world/proof substitution,
changed bounds, unavailable inputs and mutation of another family. Separate
matching/native checking verifies all 196 new proofs; independent case
arithmetic checks all 7,707 rows. The 7,407 inherited proofs are bound to
their prior verified bytes, not counted as new scientific replication.
See [the method](METHOD.md), [source bindings](SOURCES.md),
[costs](COSTS.md) and [machine summary](summary.json).

The finite construction is not exhaustive arbitrary-rectangle geometry.
No threshold, reference contract or deployment policy is chosen. Prior
conventional/native query parity and attained resolved-case query floors
stand. Savings, timed human work, genuine customer revisions and demand
remain unproven. All 1,433 reserved images remain closed. Derived results
retain [nuScenes attribution and terms](DISTRIBUTION.md); actual worlds,
source predictions and proof payloads remain private.
